into md.he
lang he
namespace md
use std
use json

This module ports a JavaScript markdown renderer and must reproduce its output exactly, quirks included, so follow every description literally. Text is UTF-8 bytes, positions are byte offsets, and input is assumed to be valid UTF-8. Output is always appended to the end of a byte buffer parameter named out. A word character is an ASCII letter, digit or underscore. Whitespace means JavaScript whitespace as measured by `space_at`. Non-ASCII characters are never word characters and are copied through whole and unchanged. A left to right scan that finds a match continues right after that match without looking inside it. A function that gives several values returns them as a calling convention result.

```he
HL_COM := "<span class=\"hl-com\">"
HL_STR := "<span class=\"hl-str\">"
HL_NUM := "<span class=\"hl-num\">"
HL_KW := "<span class=\"hl-kw\">"
HL_FN := "<span class=\"hl-fn\">"
HL_OP := "<span class=\"hl-op\">"
SPAN_END := "</span>"
A_1 := "<a href=\""
A_2 := "\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">"
A_END := "</a>"
IMG_1 := "<img src=\""
IMG_2 := "\" alt=\""
IMG_3 := "\" loading=\"lazy\">"
Q_GT := "\">"
TASK_1 := "<span class=\"task\"><input type=\"checkbox\" disabled"
TASK_CHECKED := " checked"
